6. Dataset Description
6.1 Source and provenance
The dataset is the HHS/ORR Unaccompanied Alien Children Program public operational report,
retrieved as a single CSV named HHS_Unaccompanied_Alien_Children_Program.csv and placed in
data/raw/ . It is a public aggregate extract: it contains daily counts only, with no case identifiers, no
demographic breakdowns beyond nothing at all, and no personally identifiable information. The structural
consequence — that this study is structurally incapable of privacy harm at the individual level — is
developed in Section 19.
6.2 Structure
The raw file contains 1,170 rows and 6 columns. Of these, 720 rows carry valid data and 450
rows are entirely null — a block of trailing blank lines that survived the source export. Data is
presented in reverse chronological order, with the most recent record (21 December 2025) on line 2.
The 720 valid observations span 12 January 2023 to 21 December 2025, a window of 1,075 calendar
days.
One column name carries an asterisk in the source: Children apprehended and placed in CBP custody* .
The asterisk denotes a source footnote not reproduced in the extract. Because the extract does not carry
the footnote text, the column is renamed to cbp_apprehended in the cleaned output with the semantics
recorded in Table 1 and the caveat preserved in Section 18.
