file:///C:/Users/LOQ/OneDrive/Desktop/UAC Data Care Analysis/reports/research_paper.html 10/38
7.7 Persistence
The cleaned frame is written to data/processed/ with index=False . The project currently emits two
cleaned artefacts — uac_care_cleaned.csv (from the library) and uac_cleaned.csv (from the notebook)
— both of 720 rows. See Section 18.
8. Data Quality Validation
Validation is treated as a first-class analytical stage, not as a debugging step. Three invariants are checked
and each is expressed as a column so that violations can be inspected, counted and plotted.
8.1 Invariant 1 — transfer conservation
transfer_invalid := cbp_transferred_out > cbp_in_custody
A daily transfer out of CBP custody cannot exceed the stock it is drawn from if both quantities are
measured on the same day and the stock is measured before the transfer. 86 of 720 records (11.94%)
violate this invariant.
8.2 Invariant 2 — discharge conservation
discharge_invalid := hhs_discharged > hhs_in_care
0 of 720 records violate this invariant. The discharge figure is always consistent with the population
it is drawn from, confirming that the HHS-side reporting is internally coherent.
8.3 Invariant 3 — non-negativity
No negative values occur in any of the five raw count columns. Negative values do occur in derived
difference columns, which is expected and correct: net_intake takes negative values on 475 observations,
daily_load_change on 326 and net_intake_7obs on 466. A negative derived value is a signal, not an
error.
8.4 Composite flag
data_quality_flag := transfer_invalid | discharge_invalid
86 flagged records (11.94%), identical to the transfer-violation count because the discharge set is
empty.
