8.5 Diagnosis of the transfer violations
The 86 violations are not arithmetic errors. Their structure is diagnostic:
Median CBP custody stock on violating days: 158
Median daily transfers on violating days: 182
Distribution by year: 2023 → 43; 2024 → 31; 2025 → 12
Date range: 24 January 2023 to 27 February 2025
Most recent violation: 27 February 2025 — none in the final ten months of the window
The systematic excess of transfers over the same-day stock, the presence on 12% of days, and the complete
disappearance after February 2025 all point to a definitional mismatch rather than a recording
error: the Children in CBP custody figure is a periodic administrative stock snapshot, while Children
transferred out of CBP custody is a period-total flow. When a stock is sampled less frequently than the
flow it bounds, flow totals for a period can legitimately exceed the sampled stock. The post-February-2025
cessation is consistent with a change in CBP's reporting practice, not with a change in the underlying
process.
