Option C is adopted. This is the study's general data-quality position: the defect is metadata about the
data, and the correct response is to carry it forward explicitly rather than to launder it away. The
dashboard surfaces the flag count directly so that no consumer of the analysis is unaware that 12% of
records carry it.
8.7 What the audit found that a summary statistic would not
The value of this stage is demonstrated by the missing-date audit. Had the 355 absent calendar days been
silently forward-filled with zeros — the default behaviour of a naïve resample('D').sum() — the analysis
would have reported 355 days of zero system activity and driven mean load down by roughly a third. The
33% under-reporting would have been recast as a collapse in caseload. The audit prevents that specific and
severe error, and the dashboard repeats the warning verbatim to its users.
