10.1 Design notes
min_periods=3 on all rolling windows. With 161 multi-day gaps in the series, a 7-observation window
is not a 7-day window; on this data it spans a median of roughly 10–12 calendar days. The min_periods=3
choice ensures the feature is populated from the third observation onward rather than emitting a long
ragged NaN prefix, at the cost of making the early-window values noisier. This is a deliberate
accuracy/usability trade-off, documented rather than hidden.
pct_change is used alongside absolute difference. A 1% change means something very different at a
caseload of 10,000 than at 2,000. care_load_growth_rate is the only feature in the set that is comparable
across the 2023 and 2025 regimes, and it is therefore the correct basis for any cross-period statement.
discharge_offset_ratio is retained but demoted. Its median of 1.28 is interpretable and useful, but
its maximum of 43.27 arises on days with near-zero transfers, and it is undefined on 3 observations. It is
excluded from the KPI framework for that reason and is a good illustration of a feature that is analytically
interesting but operationally fragile.
