11. KPI Framework
The following framework translates the derived features into named operational indicators. Each KPI is
defined with its formula, its update cadence, its interpretation and — critically — its failure condition, the
circumstance in which the KPI should not be trusted. The inclusion of failure conditions is a deliberate
departure from conventional KPI tables and reflects Anscombe's (1973) warning that readers of statistics
are owed the conditions under which a summary ceases to mean what it appears to mean.
