9/27/26, 12:19 PM Capacity, Flow and Pressure Dynamics in the U.S. Unaccompanied Alien Children (UAC) Care System
file:///C:/Users/LOQ/OneDrive/Desktop/UAC Data Care Analysis/reports/research_paper.html 25/38
Figure 6
Figure 6. Training period, held-out test period, and the Holt damped-trend forecast. The vertical line
marks the split. The fitted model visibly over-predicts throughout the test period because the trend it
learned in training does not continue.
14.1 Interpretation — the persistence result
The naive forecast wins by two orders of magnitude. MAE 12.0 children against 223.3 for the best
fitted model; R^2 of 0.993 against −1.396. A fitted model that produces a negative R^2 is, by definition,
worse than simply predicting the training-set mean, and all four fitted models are in that territory.
This result is reported in the paper rather than engineered away, for three reasons.
It is a direct instance of the central empirical finding of the forecasting literature. The M4
and M5 competitions established across 100,000+ time series that simple methods are competitive with
or superior to complex ones, and that combination and judgement often outperform both (Makridakis,
Spiliotis, & Assimakopoulos, 2018, 2022; Petropoulos et al., 2022). A naive-method victory on a single
series is unsurprising. What is surprising is its magnitude.
The magnitude is explained by a regime shift, and the explanation is verifiable in the
reported statistics. Training mean load is 7,221.2; test mean load is 2,278.9 — a 68.4% level difference
between the two partitions. Every model that attempts to project a trend across that boundary must carry
the 2023–2024 level into a 2025 regime that no longer contains it. Holt's damped trend, the most
conservative of the fitted models, still misses by 10.4% on average. ARIMA(1,1,1), which differences away
the level, is the most adversely affected (16.4%), and the historical mean, which is the most leveldependent, is catastrophic (218.8%).
Persistence wins here because the test period is flat. When the recent series is a near-constant
plateau, the previous value is an excellent predictor regardless of model class, and any attempt to
extrapolate a change is punished. The naive model's 0.53% MAPE is a statement about the smoothness of
the test regime, not about the superiority of the method.
9/27/26, 12:19 PM Capacity, Flow and Pressure Dynamics in the U.S. Unaccompanied Alien Children (UAC) Care System
file:///C:/Users/LOQ/OneDrive/Desktop/UAC Data Care Analysis/reports/research_paper.html 26/38
14.2 What follows for practice
Three conclusions, and one non-conclusion.
1. Deploy no fitted forecasting model to this series in its current form. The evidence does not
support it. A production system that projected 2025 load using a model trained on 2023–2024 would
over-forecast by an order of magnitude.
2. If forecasting is required, establish a regime-aware baseline first. Any serious attempt
should (a) re-derive models on recent data only, (b) evaluate with rolling-origin rather than a single
fixed split (Tashman, 2000), (c) test explicitly for structural breaks before fitting, and (d) report the
persistence baseline alongside every candidate model as a mandatory comparator. Following Hyndman
and Athanasopoulos (2021), a model that cannot beat the naive method on rolling-origin evaluation
should not be deployed.
3. Probabilistic framing may be more appropriate than point forecasting. Given the regime
instability documented in Section 9, the operationally useful output is a scenario range rather than a
point estimate. Conformal prediction (Vovk, Gammerman, & Shafer, 2005; Lei et al., 2018) and
predictive distributions (Gneiting & Katzfuss, 2014) offer principled routes to calibrated intervals
under exactly the distribution shift that defeats the point models here.
4. Non-conclusion: this study does not claim that forecasting is infeasible for this system. It claims
that these five model classes, trained on the full history and evaluated on this particular split, do not
currently deliver value. That is a much narrower claim, and it is falsifiable.
14.3 Evaluation-protocol caveat
A single 80/20 split yields one number per model and no estimate of its own uncertainty. Given that the
entire performance ordering is driven by where the split boundary happens to fall, a rolling-origin
evaluation across multiple split points is the minimum protocol required before any of these numbers is
quoted operationally. That work is out of scope here and is recorded in Section 18.
15. Streamlit Dashboard
The complete analysis is deployed as an interactive application ( app.py ) built on Streamlit 1.64.0, so that
stakeholders can interrogate the same evidence without executing Python.
15.1 Functionality
Page configuration. Wide layout, page title "UAC Care Load Analytics", captioned "Unaccompanied
Children Care System".
Cached data loading. @st.cache_data decorates the loader, so the 720-row feature table is read and
parsed once per session rather than on every widget interaction. The loader reads
data/processed/uac_features.csv with parse_dates=["Date"] .
